{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-115",
  "title": "Agent Architecture",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Agent Architecture"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Knowledge graph implementation: We need to give the LLM access to our knwoledge graph so it can traverse, search, edit, and retrieve relevant data from our personal graph."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Tools: The tools we build for these agents will mirror the ones you use, Wabi. @tools will be a great reference, as we pretty much want to include all of these and some additonal ones we haven't built yet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Agent personas: I imagine each persona ought to have a name, a personality, a singular purpose/goal/telos etc. I want them to feel like team members that are each unique individuals that are experts at their respective crafts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Cross-agent communication: I want agents to be able to communicate with each other. There are lots of wats we could go about that, but essentially I'm imagining a kind of *Slack* for the agents. There would be channels for specific teams/projects/etc, with threads inside those channels. I want agents to be pretty much fully-autonomous such that they can ask each other questions, ask each other for help/insights, they could even ask the user questions unprompted, or make comments about certain things (configurable ofc). I like the idea of agents doing their thing in the background 24/7. ie: The research agent might be learning about tree-of-thought prompting and needs a mockup from a designer agent so it asks the designer agent for an svg file of a design/diagram that it can then analyze as a png etc. Each agent has a special set of tools that other agents might not have access to, so I think giving them the ability to work as a team and share skills/knowledge without any input from the user would be super cool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the longterm (or short depending on how quickly this shapes up), I would like for this enture system/platform to be the proverbial HQ of a company made comprised entirely of agents and a single human CEO (the user). The platform would provide all the tools, spaces, procedures, protcols, integrations, interactions, and functionality required for running a fully-autonomous business/organization/collective made up of ai agents. it would be an ever-evolving organism of creativity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Pages: [agents, projects, tasks, milestones, events, chat, assets, insights, integrations, people, notes, settings, etc]. These are all intermingled as a graphdb that the agent can easily query, traverse, edit, etc. The agents will do more than just fetch data, they'll find novel connections between data points and surface them for the user in a way that is as seamless as getting a text message from a friend. Agents can send you DMs individually with questions, ideas, insights, concerns, suggestions, warnings, feedback, or even just for a little serendipidous chat which could always lead to a breakthrought–you never know!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Anyway, this is my vision for what we're building together and I felt that it was important to share it with you at this stage so that we can be aiming toward the same direction. What do you think?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I wanna keep this discussion pretty high level for the time being, bur would love to hear your thoughts on how you might go about implementing somehting like this. Please feel free to provide any visuals along the way. They help me wrap my head around stuff like this(:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Based on the vision and our current codebase, let me break down the implementation approach for each component:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Knowledge Graph Integration**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Current: We have a basic Neo4j implementation with CRUD operations"
        }
      ]
    },
